<%- include('../partials/layout-start') %>
<%- include('../partials/page-header', { icon: 'bi-shield-check', heading: 'Privacy policy' }) %>
<section class="glass-section pb-5">
<div class="container">
  <div class="row justify-content-center"><div class="col-lg-8">
    <div class="glass-card"><div class="card-body">
      <p class="text-muted-2">Version <%= version %></p>

      <h2 class="h6">What we store</h2>
      <p>Your account details, the profile you choose to publish, the applications you send, and the
         rate figures you contribute. We record the country your sign-up came from, derived offline
         from your IP address; the address itself is stored only in binary form on your account row
         and is not used for anything else.</p>

      <h2 class="h6" id="cookies">Cookies</h2>
      <%#
        Written as a statement of what exists. Without GA4 that is one cookie and the banner
        in public/js/main.js is a notice. With GA4 configured (config/webAnalytics.js) there
        are cookies a visitor can refuse, so public/js/analytics.js asks first and this
        section says so. Every sentence below is rendered only when it is true for this
        deployment, because a policy describing a tag that is not on the page — or missing
        one that is — is wrong in a document people rely on.
      %>
      <% const wa = (typeof webAnalytics !== 'undefined' && webAnalytics) || {}; %>
      <p>This site sets <strong><%= wa.ga4Id ? 'one cookie of its own' : 'one cookie' %></strong>, named <code>saphub.sid</code>. It holds a
         random session identifier and nothing else — no name, no email, no browsing history.
         It is what keeps you signed in between pages, and it is deleted when you sign out.
         Ticking "keep me signed in" only changes how long it lasts.</p>
      <% if (wa.ga4Id) { %>
      <p><strong>Google Analytics, only if you allow it.</strong> When you first visit we ask
         whether we may count your visit with Google Analytics. If you choose "Allow
         analytics", Google sets the cookies <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>, which
         keep a random identifier for up to two years so that repeat visits can be told apart,
         and the pages you open, your approximate location, device and the site that referred
         you are sent to Google, which processes them on our behalf. If you choose "Decline",
         nothing is loaded from Google and no such cookie is set. You can change your answer at
         any time with "Analytics choices" at the foot of every page; withdrawing removes the
         cookies. Your answer is kept in your browser's local storage, not in a cookie.</p>
      <p>There are no advertising cookies. The session cookie is strictly necessary for a
         function you asked for, so we do not ask you to consent to it. The in-page
         assistant keeps your conversation in your own browser's session storage, which is
         not a cookie, is never sent to us, and is gone when you close the tab.</p>
      <% } else { %>
      <p>There are no analytics cookies, no advertising cookies and no third-party cookies.
         <% if (!wa.cloudflareToken) { %>Nothing on this site is loaded from a tracker. <% } %>Because the one cookie is strictly
         necessary for a function you asked for, we do not ask you to consent to it — there
         would be nothing to decline that would leave the site working. The in-page
         assistant keeps your conversation in your own browser's session storage, which is
         not a cookie, is never sent to us, and is gone when you close the tab.</p>
      <% } %>

      <h2 class="h6" id="analytics">Visitor analytics</h2>
      <p>We count page views per country per day. No path, identifier or address is kept alongside
         that count, so it cannot be traced back to a person.</p>
      <% if (wa.cloudflareToken) { %>
      <p>We also use <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>, which runs for every visitor
         because it sets no cookie and keeps no identifier: it cannot recognise you on a
         second visit. For each page view it receives the address of the page, the site that
         referred you, your browser and device type, the country your connection comes from
         and how long the page took to load, and reports them to us only as totals.</p>
      <% } %>

      <h2 class="h6" id="reports">Messages, problem reports and ideas</h2>
      <p>When you write to us through the contact form or <a href="/report-issue">Report a problem</a>
         we store what you send: your name, your email address, the subject and message, the type and
         severity (or priority) you chose, the page address you gave, the link to any content you are
         reporting, any screenshots you attached, and — if you were signed in — which account sent it.
         We use it only to read and answer your message and to fix what you reported. We do not store
         your IP address with it.</p>
      <p>Screenshots are deleted <%= screenshotRetentionDays %> days after the report is closed: they can
         show anything that was on your screen, so we keep them only while they are useful. The message
         itself is kept as the record of what was reported and how it was answered; you can ask us to
         delete yours at any time by writing to <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">Your rate contributions</h2>
      <p>Contributions are never displayed individually. They are aggregated with other people's, and
         no aggregate is published until at least three different people have contributed to it.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">Demographic questions</h2>
      <p>Gender and date of birth are optional, used only in aggregate, never shown on your profile
         and never shared with employers. Leaving them blank has no effect on anything.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">Consent record</h2>
      <p>When you register we store the exact versions of these documents you accepted, and when. We
         do not record consent on your behalf for accounts created by an administrator.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">Deletion</h2>
      <p>Ask us and your account and its data are removed. Aggregate figures already published cannot
         single you out and are not recomputed.</p>
    </div></div>
  </div></div>
</div>
<%- include('../partials/layout-end') %>
